"Menus stop hand-rolling buttons with pre-derived props. Shared atoms take an ID plus a slot/context discriminator and look everything else up from subscribed state: GearButton(entityId, slot) derives kind, display name, stat summary, on-state, disablement+reason, and the slot's proposal; PoolActionButton(actionId, bar) likewise; ActionsBarEditor resolves names internally (drop the nameOf prop). ONE useInstanceIsOn(entityId, slot) hook replaces the three current counted-rule derivations (useTargetIsEquipped, LoadoutPanel inline, StancesMenu isOn) so highlights and option rules can never disagree. Gear display names route through a vocabulary like actions do (closes menus-render-display-names-not-internal-keys for gear). Rationale: every menu inconsistency so far (duplicate-armor highlight, missing disablement, divergent grip bases, raw asset keys, summary-less stance buttons) traces to per-site derivation that shared atoms make impossible."